Probabilistic verification of ensemble brightness temperature (Tb) forecasts
============================================================================

Verifies an ensemble of Tb forecasts in observation space against geostationary
IR observations (e.g., ABI on GOES-16, AHI on Himawari-8), using the per-member
obsout files written by the MPAS-Workflow forecast verification.

Method
------
For each forecast initialization time, lead time, and threshold:
  1. An event is Tb below (default; cold, cloudy) or above the threshold, defined
     for the obs and for each member at every location.
  2. The forecast probability is the fraction of members forecasting the event.
  3. An Nx2 contingency table (forecast probability bin x observed yes/no) is written out.
The tables are summed over initialization times, and from the aggregated tables:
  - Reliability diagram: observed relative frequency vs. forecast probability (bin center),
    with the sample count per bin in an inset.
  - ROC curve and the area under it (AUC), using each probability bin edge as a decision threshold.
  - Brier score (BS) and Brier skill score (BSS = 1 - BS/BS_clim), where
    BS_clim = obar*(1-obar) and obar is the observed event frequency of the sample
    (sample climatology, per lead time and threshold). For pct_<p>, obar = p/100; for val_<v>,
    obar can change with lead time.
  As in MET, BS and the reliability diagram use the center of each probability bin as the
  forecast probability, computed from the Nx2 contingency table.

Thresholds (-thres, comma-separated):
  pct_<p>  p-th percentile, computed separately for the obs and for each member. The obs and
           every member then have the same event frequency, so a systematic Tb bias does not
           affect the scores. The physical value of each threshold is saved in the case tables.
  val_<v>  fixed Tb in K.

Probability bins (-nbins, default 20): bin 0 is [0, 1/nbins], bin i is (i/nbins, (i+1)/nbins].
Bins are assigned from member counts, so there is no round-off at the bin edges. With fewer
members than bins, some bins are empty; they are skipped in the plots.

Locations where the obs or any member's hofx is missing are removed from that case. A case
with a missing member file is skipped, and is not counted in the aggregation (nCases).

Files
-----
probabilisticVerification.py  Driver: reads the members, writes the tables, makes the plots.
probutils.py                  Thresholds, contingency tables, aggregation, and scores.
plot.py                       Plotting functions (maps, histograms, reliability, ROC, lead time).
qsub.sh                       Submits one PBS job per channel. Edit the VARIABLES SETUP section.
utils.py                      Link to ../conditionalVerification/utils.py (dates, argument parsing, logging).
plot_abi_L2_direct.py         Standalone: plots ABI L2 cloud products from NOAA CLASS at their
                              original resolution. Expensive.

Input
-----
Member files are found from a template (-tmpl), by default
  {expDir}/Verification/fc/mem{mem:03d}/{init}/{fhr}hr/dbOut/obsout_{app}_{sensor}.h5
where {expDir} is the experiment directory (-dir), {mem} the member number, {init} the
initialization date (YYYYMMDDHH), {fhr} the lead time in hours, {app} is -app (default hofx),
and {sensor} is -s (default abi_g16).
The number of members is counted from the files unless -nmem is given. The channel (-ch) is
the value of the Channel coordinate in the file, e.g. 13 for the ABI/AHI 10.4/10.3 um band.

Usage
-----
module load conda && conda activate npl
export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1   # avoid __pycache__/ in the repository

python probabilisticVerification.py -dir <experiment dir> -s abi_g16 -ch 13 \
    -di 2018041500 -de 2018051200 -dt 72 -fhr0 6 -fhr 48 -freq 6 \
    -thres pct_5.0,pct_10.0,pct_20.0,val_235.0 [-maps true] [-hist true] [-cases true]

Run with -h for all options. Useful ones:
  -maps true      obs Tb, ensemble mean and spread, obs event, and forecast probability maps per case
  -ens true       a map for every member (expensive)
  -hist true      obs and ensemble hofx Tb histograms per case
  -cases true     reliability and ROC plots per case
  -ev below|above event is Tb below (default) or above the threshold
  -plotOnly true  re-plot the scores from existing aggregated tables, without reading the members.
                  -dir, -di, and -de are still required, and the lead times (-fhr0, -fhr, -freq)
                  and thresholds (-thres) must match the original run to find the tables.
  -ext lon0,lon1,lat0,lat1   map extent (default: global)
  -np N           number of processes computing the tables and plots of each case
                  (default: all available cpus)
  -nread N        number of processes reading member files (default 16). Reading is I/O bound,
                  so N can exceed the number of cpus. Reads overlap within and across cases.

On Derecho/Casper, edit the VARIABLES SETUP section of qsub.sh and run ./qsub.sh from this
directory (it finds probabilisticVerification.py in the current directory). For each channel,
it creates an output folder <sensor>_ch<ch>_<dateIni>-<dateEnd>_<fhr>hr/ in this directory and
submits the job from there.

plot_abi_L2_direct.py (standalone):
python plot_abi_L2_direct.py -obs <dir with data_from_noaa_class_<product>/> \
    -latlon <dir with latlon_<resol>.nc> -di 2018041600 -de 2018041600 [-p CTPF,ACHAF] [-np N]

Output (under -o, default the current directory)
------
tables/contingency_table_i<init>_f<hhh>_v<valid>_<thres>.yaml   per case, with the physical thresholds
tables/contingency_table_aggregated_f<hhh>_<thres>.yaml         summed over initialization times
scores/reliability_*.png, scores/roc_*.png
    aggregated_<ch>_f<hhh>_<thres>      one lead time and threshold
    aggregated_summary_<ch>_f<hhh>      all thresholds for one lead time
    aggregated_summary_<ch>_<thres>     all lead times for one threshold
    i<init>_f<hhh>_v<valid>_<thres>     one case (-cases true)
scores/{BS,BSS,AUC}_aggregated_summary_<ch>.png   as a function of lead time, one line per threshold
scores/scores_aggregated_summary_<ch>.yaml        the BS, BSS, and AUC values
maps/                                             maps and histograms (-maps, -ens, -hist)

log.verification (log file) is written to the current directory, not under -o.

Contingency table format (YAML):
  nBins, nMembers, nCases
  obsYes, obsNo   count of locations per probability bin where the event was / was not observed
  physicalThreshold: {obs, members}   (per case only)
